1
00:00:00,560 --> 00:00:05,460
Stone Age emotions. Medieval institutions. Godlike technology.

2
00:00:06,460 --> 00:00:15,180
This is not a bug. It's the operating system. And the operating system is trying to kill you with nuclear weapons and preventable

3
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:23,200
disease simultaneously. The Selfish Gene Made You Illogical (It Was a Good Idea at the Time).

4
00:00:24,220 --> 00:00:32,860
Richard Dawkins put it perfectly: "We are survival machines, robot vehicles blindly programmed to preserve the selfish molecules

5
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:42,680
known as genes.". Translation: You're a meat puppet controlled by chemicals whose entire business plan is "make more chemicals

6
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:47,480
before something eats us.". Your genes don't care if you're happy.

7
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:55,680
They don't care if you live past 30. They care about exactly one thing: making copies of themselves before something with

8
00:00:55,680 --> 00:01:02,700
teeth finds you. For ninety-nine point nine percent of human history, this was brilliant engineering.

9
00:01:03,340 --> 00:01:10,580
Now it's why you distrust strangers you need to cooperate with, build weapons you'll never use, and fight over territory

10
00:01:10,580 --> 00:01:15,280
you don't need. The genes are still celebrating. You are not.

11
00:01:16,320 --> 00:01:20,560
Part 1: Your Brain Was Optimized for a World That Doesn't Exist.

12
00:01:21,960 --> 00:01:26,880
The Violence Module (Or: Why You Tend to Prefer Bombs Over Band-Aids).

13
00:01:27,820 --> 00:01:32,450
Fifteen to thirty percent of your ancestors died from violence.

14
00:01:32,540 --> 00:01:41,200
Not disease. Not starvation. Other humans, smashing their heads with rocks over territorial disputes about berry bushes.

15
00:01:41,820 --> 00:01:48,200
You've since upgraded the rocks to intercontinental ballistic missiles, but the berry bush energy remains.

16
00:01:48,720 --> 00:01:52,220
The tribes that survived weren't the peaceful, loving ones.

17
00:01:52,720 --> 00:02:00,460
They were the paranoid, survival-focused ones who: Assumed every stranger might want to kill them (often statistically accurate).

18
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:08,690
Struck first when threatened (natural selection at work). Formed tight combat groups to kill other groups (teamwork!).

19
00:02:09,660 --> 00:02:13,620
Hoarded weapons obsessively (can never have too many pointy sticks).

20
00:02:14,580 --> 00:02:21,920
Your brain is still running this exact software. That's why: You spend more preparing to kill each other than preparing

21
00:02:21,920 --> 00:02:27,060
to not die. You instinctively distrust people who don't look like your tribe.

22
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:32,900
Twitter arguments feel like actual combat (your amygdala can't tell the difference).

23
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:38,460
Countries with ten thousand nuclear weapons are worried they don't have enough.

24
00:02:39,380 --> 00:02:43,560
The violence module kept your ancestors from getting clubbed to death.

25
00:02:43,820 --> 00:02:47,180
Now it's building weapons that could end all life on Earth.

26
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:52,960
Computer scientists call this "feature creep." Biologists call it "maladaptive."

27
00:02:53,460 --> 00:03:02,060
I call it "the reason I'm writing this book.". The Tribal Brain (Or: Why Democracy Was Always Going to Be a Mess).

28
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:09,080
Dunbar's number says humans can maintain stable relationships with about one hundred and fifty people.

29
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:17,300
That's your entire social capacity. Your brain has one hundred and fifty slots for caring about people, and you've filled

30
00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:22,160
most of them with coworkers you tolerate and celebrities who don't know you exist.

31
00:03:22,920 --> 00:03:29,800
Your brain treats anything outside your one hundred and fifty-person monkeysphere as an abstraction.

32
00:03:29,880 --> 00:03:36,320
That's why: You care more about your neighbor's barking dog than ten thousand people dying of malaria (the dog is RIGHT

33
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:40,830
THERE being loud, malaria is just a concept with numbers attached).

34
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:47,760
Local corruption makes you angrier than trillion-dollar Pentagon waste (the local guy stole ten thousand dollars you can

35
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:53,230
imagine, the Pentagon lost two point five trillion dollars which is just syllables).

36
00:03:54,400 --> 00:04:01,900
You'll donate to save one sick child but ignore statistics about millions (one child has a face, millions is just a very

37
00:04:01,900 --> 00:04:08,180
big number that makes your brain hurt). Democracy asks this brain to make civilization-level decisions.

38
00:04:08,920 --> 00:04:13,040
It goes exactly as well as asking a labrador retriever to do your taxes.

39
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:18,459
You vote based on: Who looks stronger (your brain thinks the election is a wrestling match).

40
00:04:19,320 --> 00:04:26,860
Who your tribe likes (if the clan approves, must be good). Who makes you feel safe (fear sells better than policy ever will).

41
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:31,760
Who you'd have a beer with (relevance to nuclear policy: zero).

42
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:38,140
You elect leaders using the same brain circuits your ancestors used to pick the guy with the biggest club.

43
00:04:39,100 --> 00:04:46,520
Part 2: Genetic Slavery is Literally Killing Us. Evolution prepared you for scarcity, predators, and violence.

44
00:04:47,280 --> 00:04:54,720
You got abundance, safety, and Netflix. Your bodies responded with the biological equivalent of a computer trying to print

45
00:04:54,720 --> 00:05:01,350
a sandwich. Here's the cosmic joke: Humanity has never been safer, healthier, or more prosperous.

46
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:08,560
You've also never been closer to wiping itself out. You solved poverty and invented nuclear war in the same century.

47
00:05:09,260 --> 00:05:16,910
Very on-brand. Problems you solved. Starvation (you throw away forty percent of food because storing it is inconvenient).

48
00:05:17,860 --> 00:05:23,440
Predators (you murdered them into extinction, then put them in zoos so your children could see what you killed).

49
00:05:24,220 --> 00:05:30,980
Infant mortality (basically eradicated in developed countries, which makes the death rate in poor countries feel more optional

50
00:05:31,260 --> 00:05:37,260
and thus more tragic). Most infectious diseases (vaccines work despite what Facebook says).

51
00:05:38,020 --> 00:05:45,740
Dying at thirty (now you complain about turning forty, which your ancestors would consider a miracle worth celebrating daily).

52
00:05:46,320 --> 00:05:54,220
New problems you invented with your big brains: Nuclear weapons (enough to end civilization twenty times because once wasn't

53
00:05:54,220 --> 00:05:59,500
enough). Climate change (you're terraforming your only planet by accident).

54
00:06:00,340 --> 00:06:07,140
Antibiotic resistance (ten million deaths annually by twenty fifty because you gave antibiotics to cows).

55
00:06:07,860 --> 00:06:12,280
A.I. that might become sentient and decide you're the problem (the A.I.

56
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:18,960
would be correct). Social media (voluntary psychological torture you pay for with attention).

57
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:26,640
Eight billion gene copies and counting. From evolution's perspective, an unqualified triumph.

58
00:06:26,680 --> 00:06:33,320
You're just the disposable meat robot they used to do it. Humanity is a toddler who found the nuclear launch codes.

59
00:06:34,020 --> 00:06:37,700
Godlike technological power, hamster-level impulse control.

60
00:06:38,700 --> 00:06:46,120
Part 3: Why You Can't Just "Be Better". Your conscious mind controls maybe five percent of your decisions.

61
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:51,840
The other ninety-five percent is your ancient lizard brain running software older than agriculture.

62
00:06:52,520 --> 00:06:57,660
You think you're the pilot. You're actually a passenger who occasionally gets to suggest a direction.

63
00:06:58,400 --> 00:07:05,980
This scales to civilization. Your brain's fear center (amygdala) is directly connected to your voting finger.

64
00:07:06,980 --> 00:07:14,920
Politicians know this. Say "terrorism" and your lizard brain overrides everything: More people die from falling out of bed

65
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:19,140
than terrorism. You're one thousand times more likely to die from heart disease.

66
00:07:20,060 --> 00:07:28,160
But terrorism *feels* scarier, because evolution optimized your fear response for things with faces, not things with cholesterol.

67
00:07:29,160 --> 00:07:34,720
The fear of violent death is older than language. The fear of slow death from disease?

68
00:07:35,180 --> 00:07:40,890
Your brain files that under "boring, deal with later." Later never comes.

69
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:48,220
Neither does the cure. That's why you spent two point seven two trillion dollars on weapons while cancer research got pocket

70
00:07:48,220 --> 00:07:54,880
change. Your bed is more dangerous than Al-Qaeda, but nobody's declared a War on Furniture.

71
00:07:55,840 --> 00:08:00,840
Part 4: Breaking the Chains. Every single one of you is going to die.

72
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:08,700
From the most powerful president to the lowliest pauper, you face a life of gradually escalating suffering until it ends.

73
00:08:09,480 --> 00:08:17,820
This is not a warning. It's a weather report. You can feed everyone twice over, but you'd rather burn grain to keep prices

74
00:08:17,820 --> 00:08:25,120
high. You can cure diseases, but you'd rather sell treatments forever (cured customers don't come back; bad for quarterly

75
00:08:25,120 --> 00:08:32,799
earnings). You could be immortal space wizards. Instead you're cave-dwelling murderers with better tools.

76
00:08:33,539 --> 00:08:38,460
Because the current system makes irrationality profitable. Spectacularly profitable.

77
00:08:39,419 --> 00:08:42,580
Every bomb makes someone rich. Every missile funds a yacht.

78
00:08:43,020 --> 00:08:47,120
Every war creates a billionaire. Disease is profitable too.

79
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:55,600
Not curing it, treating it. Insulin costs three hundred dollars a vial because dead diabetics don't buy insulin.

80
00:08:56,300 --> 00:09:00,560
But cured diabetics don't either. So you keep them barely alive.

81
00:09:01,020 --> 00:09:06,100
It's good business. The people making money from war and disease aren't evil.

82
00:09:06,460 --> 00:09:10,180
They're just rational actors in a system that rewards the wrong things.

83
00:09:10,900 --> 00:09:16,820
You can't change human nature. Two hundred thousand years of evolution doesn't care about your TED talk.

84
00:09:17,420 --> 00:09:23,160
But you can create economic systems that make curing people more profitable than killing them.

85
00:09:23,640 --> 00:09:27,280
That's the only upgrade your species has ever responded to.

86
00:09:28,300 --> 00:09:36,600
Expecting a brain built for hunting gazelles to handle nuclear policy, climate change, and a global economy is like expecting

87
00:09:36,600 --> 00:09:41,420
a calculator to run a space program. The calculator isn't broken.

88
00:09:41,820 --> 00:09:44,660
You're just asking it to do something it was never built for.

89
00:09:45,220 --> 00:09:50,240
You can't fight two hundred thousand years of evolution. But you can hack it.

90
00:09:50,920 --> 00:09:58,640
That's what a one percent treaty does. Instead of asking people to be rational (impossible), use their irrational impulses:

91
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:03,280
Greed: Make curing disease more profitable than building bombs.

92
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:07,280
Fear: Make politicians more scared of voters than lobbyists.

93
00:10:08,220 --> 00:10:12,170
Tribalism: Create an us-versus-disease tribe instead of us-versus-them.

94
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:16,720
Social proof: Get three point five percent participation so others follow.

95
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:26,700
Immediate rewards: Pay people cash to join medical trials. Your genes enslaved you in brains that fear strangers and cannot

96
00:10:26,700 --> 00:10:31,690
comprehend statistics. But they also gave you the ability to see the prison.

97
00:10:32,360 --> 00:10:36,700
No other animal can think: "Wow, my instincts are completely illogical."

98
00:10:37,620 --> 00:10:43,820
That's uniquely human. Use it. A one percent treaty doesn't ask you to be better.

99
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:49,260
It assumes you won't be, and redirects your worst impulses toward not dying.

100
00:10:49,820 --> 00:10:56,100
It's the only plan that works for the species you actually are, rather than the species you wish you were.
